            element_info: Some((
                atomic_number: 25,
                atomic_weight: 54.938044,
                group: Some(7),
                period: Some(4),
                block: Some("d"),
                electron_config: Some("[Ar] 3d5 4s2"),
                electronegativity_pauling: Some(1.55),
                first_ionization_kj_mol: Some(717.27315643),
                electron_affinity_kj_mol: Some(0.0),
                atomic_radius_pm: Some(140.0),
                discoverer: Some("Johann Gahn"),
                discovery_year: Some(1774),
                overview: Some("Manganese is a chemical element; it has symbol Mn and atomic number 25. It is a hard, brittle, silvery metal, often found in minerals in combination with iron. First isolated in the 1770s, manganese is a transition metal with many industrial alloy uses, particularly in stainless steels. It improves strength, workability, and resistance to wear. Manganese oxide is used as an oxidising agent, as a rubber additive, and in glass making, fertilizers, and ceramics. Manganese sulfate can be used as a fungicide.

Manganese is also an essential human dietary element, important in macronutrient metabolism, bone formation, and free radical defense systems. It is a critical component in dozens of proteins and enzymes. It is found mostly in the bones, but also the liver, kidneys, and brain. In the human brain, manganese is bound to manganese metalloproteins, most notably glutamine synthetase in astrocytes."),
                discovery_story: None,
                isotopes_summary: Some("31 known isotopes; stable: 55Mn (100.0%), 43Mn, 44Mn, 45Mn; 24 radioactive"),
                magnetic_ordering: None,
            )),
        ),
