            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsBase],
            description: Some("Benzylamine, also known as phenylmethylamine, is an organic chemical compound with the condensed structural formula C6H5CH2NH2 (sometimes abbreviated as PhCH2NH2 or BnNH2).  It consists of a benzyl group, C6H5CH2, attached to an amine functional group, NH2. This colorless water-soluble liquid is a common precursor in organic chemistry and used in the industrial production of many pharmaceuticals.  The hydrochloride salt was used to treat motion sickness on the Mercury-Atlas 6 mission in which NASA astronaut John Glenn became the first American to orbit the Earth."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H314: Causes severe skin burns and eye damage [Danger Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
            uses: ["All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "In organic synthesis", "Intermediate"],
