            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Benzaldehyde (C6H5CHO) is an organic compound consisting of a benzene ring with a formyl substituent. It is among the simplest aromatic aldehydes and one of the most industrially useful.
It is a colorless liquid with a characteristic odor similar to that of bitter almonds and cherry, and is commonly used in cherry-flavored sodas. A component of bitter almond oil, benzaldehyde can be extracted from a number of other natural sources. Synthetic benzaldehyde is the flavoring agent in imitation almond extract, which is used to flavor cakes and other baked goods."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H372: Causes damage to organs through prolonged or repeated exposure [Danger Specific target organ toxicity, repeated exposure]"),
            uses: ["Fragrance", "Fuels and fuel additives", "Intermediates", "Odor agents", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(1.499),
            appearance: Some("Benzaldehyde appears as a clear colorless to yellow liquid with a bitter almond odor. Flash point near 145 °F. More denser than water and insoluble in water. Hence sinks in water. Vapors are heavier than air. The primary hazard is to the environment. Immediate steps should be taken to limit spread to the environment. Easily penetrates the soil to contaminate groundwater and nearby waterways. Used in flavoring and perfume making."),
            synonyms: ["BEZ", "Benzylaldehyde", "Phenylmethanal", "Benzanoaldehyde", "Benzenecarbonal", "Benzenemethylal", "benzoyl hydride", "Benzoic aldehyde"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=19217866"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/240"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_17169"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q372524"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C100527&Units=SI")],
            element_info: None,
        ),
