            description: Some("4,4-Oxydianiline is a colorless, odorless, combustible aromatic amine that emits toxic fumes of nitrogen oxides when heated to decomposition. 4,4'-Oxydianiline is used in industry in the manufacture of polyimide and polyester resins. Exposure to this substance is irritating to the eyes, skin and respiratory-tract. 4,4'-Oxydianiline is reasonably anticipated to be a human carcinogen. (NCI05)"),
