            properties: [IsBase],
            description: Some("Triallylamine is the organic compound with the formula N(CH2CH=CH2)3. It is a colorless liquid with an ammonia-like odor. It is multifunctional, featuring a tertiary amine and three alkene groups.   Triallylamine (and mono- and diallyl amines) is produced by the treating allyl chloride with ammonia. 
Allylamines have particularly weak α-CH bonds, being near 80 kcal/mol."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H311+H331 (63%): Toxic in contact with skin or if inhaled. [Danger Acute toxicity, dermal; acute toxicity, inhalation]"),
            uses: ["Intermediate", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "Paper Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(1.846),
            appearance: Some("Triallylamine appears as a colorless liquid with a fishlike odor. Density 0.800 g / cm3 and insoluble in water. Hence floats on water. Flash point 103 °F. Vapors heavier than air. May irritate skin and eyes. Used to make other chemicals."),
            synonyms: ["N,N-bis(prop-2-enyl)prop-2-en-1-amine", "102-70-5", "Tris(2-propenyl)amine", "2-Propen-1-amine, N,N-di-2-propenyl-", "2-Propen-1-amine, N,N-di-2-propen-1-yl-", "N,N-Di-2-propenyl-2-propen-1-amine", "B6N19XC04R", "DTXSID5026174"],
