            description: Some("Octyl acetate, or octyl ethanoate, is an organic compound with the formula CH3(CH2)7O2CCH3.  It is classified as an ester that is formed from 1-octanol (octyl alcohol) and acetic acid. It is found in oranges, grapefruits, and other citrus products.
