            properties: [IsAcid],
            description: Some("2-Phenylethyl bromide is an organobromide with the formula C6H5CH2CH2Br.  It is a colorless liquid, although older samples appear yellow.  Analogous to the preparation of most 1-bromoalkanes, it is prepared by free-radical addition of hydrogen bromide to styrene.  These conditions lead to anti-Markovnikov addition, giving the 1-bromo derivatives.
Upon reaction with hydrazine, phenelzine is produced.
It can be used to produce fentanyl and is on the Special Surveillance List of the DEA."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H302 (98.9%): Harmful if swallowed [Warning Acute toxicity, oral]"),
