            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Propyl propanoate (also known as propyl propionate and n-propyl propionate) is the organic compound with the molecular formula C6H12O2.  It is the ester of propanol and propionic acid. Like most esters, propyl propanoate is a colorless liquid with a fruity odor.  The scent of propyl propionate is described as a chemically tinged pineapple or pear. It is used in perfumery and as a solvent. The refractive index at 20 °C is  1.393.
Because propyl propanoate is a low-odor, moderately volatile ester solvent that is not a hazardous air pollutant (HAP), with good solvent activity and versatility, it is considered a safer substitute for toluene."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H226: Flammable liquid and vapor [Warning Flammable liquids]"),
            uses: ["All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "Intermediate", "Paint and Coating Manufacturing", "Solvent", "Transportation Equipment Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(1.35),
            appearance: Some("Liquid"),
            synonyms: ["FEMA 2958", "Propyl propanoate", "n-Propyl propanoate", "n-Propyl propionate", "n-Propyl n-propionate", "Propanoic acid, propyl ester", "Propionic acid, propyl ester", "Propionic acid n-propyl ester"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=20772601"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/7803"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_89828"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q3119221"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C106365&Units=SI")],
