            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("1,3-Butadiene ( ) is an organic compound with the formula CH2=CH-CH=CH2. It is a colorless gas that is easily condensed to a liquid. It is important industrially as a precursor to synthetic rubber. The molecule can be viewed as the union of two vinyl groups. It is the simplest conjugated diene.
Although butadiene breaks down quickly in the atmosphere, it is nevertheless found in ambient air in urban and suburban areas as a consequence of its constant emission from motor vehicles.
The name butadiene can also refer to the isomer, 1,2-butadiene, which is a cumulated diene with structure H2C=C=CH−CH3. This allene has no industrial significance."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H220: Extremely flammable gas [Danger Flammable gases]"),
            uses: ["metal articles", "or plastic articles (hard)"],
            logp: Some(1.358),
            appearance: None,
            synonyms: ["HCBD", "bivinyl", "divinyl", "butadiene", "erythrene", "biethylene", "vinylethylene", "buta-1,3-diene"],
