            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Acrylonitrile is an organic compound with the formula CH2CHCN and the structure H2C=CH−C≡N. It is a colorless, volatile liquid. It has a pungent odor of garlic or onions.  Its molecular structure consists of a vinyl group (−CH=CH2) linked to a nitrile (−C≡N).  It is an important monomer for the manufacture of useful plastics such as polyacrylonitrile.  It is reactive and toxic at low doses. 
Acrylonitrile is one of the components of ABS plastic (acrylonitrile butadiene styrene)."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H225: Highly Flammable liquid and vapor [Danger Flammable liquids]"),
            uses: ["All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(0.696),
            appearance: Some("Acrylonitrile, stabilized appears as a clear colorless liquid with a strong pungent odor. Flash point 32 °F. Prolonged exposure to the vapors or skin contact harmful. Density 6.7 lb / gal. Vapors heavier than air. Combustion produces toxic oxides of nitrogen. Requires storage and handling in closed systems. Used in insecticides and to make plastics, fibers and other chemicals.   Rate of onset: Immediate  Persistence: Minutes to hours  Odor threshold: 17 ppm  Source/use/other hazard: Plastics, coatings, adhesives industries; dyes; pharmaceuticals; flam gas."),
            synonyms: ["AN", "VCN", "Ventox", "Acritet", "Acrylon", "Carbacryl", "Fumigrain", "Acrylnitril"],
