            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Toluene (), also known as toluol (), is a substituted aromatic hydrocarbon with the chemical formula C6H5CH3, often abbreviated as PhCH3, where Ph stands for the phenyl group. It is a colorless, water-insoluble liquid with the odor associated with paint thinners. It is a mono-substituted benzene derivative, consisting of a methyl group (CH3) attached to a phenyl group by a single bond. As such, its systematic IUPAC name is methylbenzene. Toluene is predominantly used as an industrial feedstock and a solvent.
As the solvent in some types of paint thinner, permanent markers, contact cement and certain types of glue, toluene is sometimes used as a recreational inhalant and has the potential of causing severe neurological harm."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H225: Highly Flammable liquid and vapor [Danger Flammable liquids]"),
            uses: ["Adhesion/cohesion promoter", "Adhesives and sealant chemicals", "Anti-adhesive/cohesive", "Catalyst", "Corrosion inhibitor", "Defoamer"],
            logp: Some(1.995),
            appearance: Some("Toluene appears as a clear colorless liquid with a characteristic aromatic odor. Flash point 40 °F. Less dense than water (7.2 lb / gal) and insoluble in water. Hence floats on water. Vapors heavier than air. May be toxic by inhalation, ingestion or skin contact. Used in aviation and automotive fuels, as a solvent, and to make other chemicals."),
            synonyms: ["Toluen", "Toluol", "methylbenzol", "methylbenzene", "phenylmethane", "phenyl-methane", "1-methylbenzene", "monomethyl benzene"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=30699"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/1140"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_17578"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q15779"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C108883&Units=SI")],
            element_info: None,
        ),
