            description: Some("3,4-Dihydropyran (DHP) is a heterocyclic compound with the formula C5H8O. The six-membered C5O ring has the unsaturation adjacent to oxygen. The isomeric 3,6-dihydropyran has a methylene separating the double bond and oxygen.  DHP is used for protecting group for alcohols.  It is a colorless liquid."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H225 (100%): Highly Flammable liquid and vapor [Danger Flammable liquids]"),
            uses: ["All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "Intermediate", "Pharmaceutical and Medicine Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(1.31),
            appearance: Some("Dihydro-2h-pyran appears as a clear colorless liquid with an ethereal odor. Less dense than water. Vapors heavier than air."),
