            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Lauroyl chloride is the organic compound with the formula CH3(CH2)10COCl.  It is the acid chloride of lauric acid.  Lauroyl chloride is a standard reagent for installing the lauroyl group.  It is mainly produced as a precursor to dilauroyl peroxide, which is widely used in free-radical polymerizations.
Lauroyl chloride is a substrate for diverse reactions characteristic of acid chlorides.  With base, it converts to laurone, a ketone with the formula [CH3(CH2)10]2CO.  With sodium azide, it reacts to give undecyl isocyanate via a Curtius rearrangement of the acyl azide."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H314 (99.5%): Causes severe skin burns and eye damage [Danger Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
            uses: ["Intermediate", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(4.673),
