            description: Some("2-Methylbutanoic acid, also known as 2-methylbutyric acid is a branched-chain alkyl carboxylic acid with the chemical formula CH3CH2CH(CH3)CO2H, classified as a short-chain fatty acid. It exists in two enantiomeric forms, (R)- and (S)-2-methylbutanoic acid.  (R)-2-methylbutanoic acid occurs naturally in cocoa beans and (S)-2-methylbutanoic occurs in many fruits such as apples and apricots, as well as in the scent of the orchid Luisia curtisii."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H314 (100%): Causes severe skin burns and eye damage [Danger Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
            uses: ["Intermediate"],
            logp: Some(1.117),
            appearance: Some("Liquid"),
            synonyms: ["2-methybutyric acid", "2-methylbutyric acid", "2-ethylpropionic acid", "ethylmethylacetic acid", "methylethylacetic acid", "DL-2-methylbutyric acid", "(R)-2-methylbutyric acid", "alpha-methylbutyric acid"],
