            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Benzophenone is a naturally occurring organic compound with the formula (C6H5)2CO, generally abbreviated Ph2CO. Benzophenone has been found in some fungi, fruits and plants, including grapes. It is a white solid with a low melting point and rose-like odor that is soluble in organic solvents. Benzophenone is the simplest diaromatic ketone. It is a widely used building block in organic chemistry, being the parent diarylketone."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H350: May cause cancer [Danger Carcinogenicity]"),
            uses: ["Intermediates", "Photosensitive agent", "Process regulators", "Semiconductor and photovoltaic agent", "Adhesive Manufacturing"],
