            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Isobornyl acetate is an organic compound consisting of the acetate ester or the terpenoid isoborneol.  It is a colorless liquid with a pleasant pine-like scent, and it is produced on a multi-ton scale for this purpose. The compound is prepared by reaction of camphene with acetic acid in the presence of a strongly acidic catalyst such as sulfuric acid. Hydrolysis of isobornyl acetate gives isoborneol, a precursor to camphor.
Like many plant exudates, isobornyl acetate appears to have antifeedant properties."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
