            solubility_g_per_100ml_h2o: None,
            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Oxybenzone or benzophenone-3 or BP-3 (trade names Milestab 9, Eusolex 4360, Escalol 567, KAHSCREEN BZ-3) is an organic compound belonging to the class of aromatic ketones known as benzophenones. It takes the form of pale-yellow crystals that are readily soluble in most organic solvents. It is widely used in sunscreen formulations, plastics, toys, furniture finishes, and other products to limit UV degradation. In nature, it can be found in various flowering plants (angiosperms). The compound was first synthesised in Germany by chemists König and Kostanecki in 1906.
The use of oxybenzone as sunscreen ingredient is currently under scrutiny by the scientific community due to controversies about the molecule's environmental impact and safety profile (see section below). As a result, sunscreens containing oxybenzone have been banned from sale in Hawaii, Palau, and Thailand."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H315 (70.2%): Causes skin irritation [Warning Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
            uses: ["Adsorbents and absorbents", "Fragrance", "Photosensitive chemicals", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(2.632),
            appearance: Some("2-hydroxy-4-methoxybenzophenone appears as white to off-white or light yellow powder. (NTP, 1992)"),
            synonyms: ["Oxibenzona", "Oxybenzone", "Uvinul M40", "Oxybenzonum", "Benzophenone-3", "2-Benzoyl-5-methoxyphenol", "4-Methoxy-2-hydroxybenzophenone", "2-(4-methoxybenzoyl)benzoic acid"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=287585"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/4632"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_174360"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q518114"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C131577&Units=SI")],
            element_info: None,
        ),
