            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsMetal],
            description: Some("Sodium oxide is a chemical compound with the formula Na2O. It is used in ceramics and glasses. It is a white solid but the compound is rarely encountered. Instead \"sodium oxide\" is used to describe components of various materials such as glasses and fertilizers which contain oxides that include sodium and other elements. Sodium oxide is a component."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H314 (86.9%): Causes severe skin burns and eye damage [Danger Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
            uses: ["Adsorbent", "Dehydrating agent (desiccant)", "Intermediates", "Adsorbents and absorbents", "All Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(-0.83),
            appearance: Some("Sodium monoxide appears as a white granular material. It reacts with water to give sodium hydroxide with the evolution of heat. It is corrosive to metals and tissue. It is used in chemical manufacture."),
            synonyms: ["H2CrO4", "Disodium oxide", "sodium chromate", "Disodium chromate", "Sodium chromate(VI)", "Chromiumsodium oxide", "Chromium disodium oxide", "Chromic acid, disodium salt"],
