            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsAcid],
            description: Some("FRD-903 (also known as hexafluoropropylene oxide dimer acid, HFPO-DA, and 2,3,3,3-tetrafluoro-2-(heptafluoropropoxy)propanoic acid) is a chemical compound that is among the class of per- and polyfluoroalkyl substances (PFASs). More specifically, this synthetic petrochemical is also described as a perfluoroalkyl ether carboxylic acid (PFECA) and a Fluorointermediate. It is not biodegradable and is not hydrolyzed by water."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H314 (59.3%): Causes severe skin burns and eye damage [Danger Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
