            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Aluminium nitrate is a chemical compound of aluminum.  It is used in tanning leather, antiperspirants, corrosion inhibitors, extraction of uranium, petroleum refining, and as a nitrating agent. Aluminum is the most abundant metal in the earth's crust and is always found combined with other elements such as oxygen, silicon, and fluorine.  Nitrite is a toxic compound known to cause methemoglobinemia. (L1137, L739, L740, L765)"),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H301 (24.3%): Toxic if swallowed [Danger Acute toxicity, oral]"),
            uses: ["Catalyst", "Adhesion/cohesion promoter", "All Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing", "Computer and Electronic Product Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(-0.729),
            appearance: Some("Aluminum nitrate appears as a white, crystalline solid. Noncombustible but can accelerate the burning of combustible materials. If large quantities are involved or the combustible material is finely divided, an explosion may result. Prolonged exposure to fire or heat may result in an explosion. Fires that involve this material, produce oxides of nitrogen. Uses include, petroleum refining, dyeing, and leather tanning."),
            synonyms: ["aluminium nitrate", "aluminium trinitrate", "aluminum(III) nitrate", "nitric acid aluminum salt", "nitric acid, aluminum salt", "nitric acid, aluminum salt (3:1)", "13473-90-0", "Aluminum trinitrate"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=3809994"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/54611382"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_231496"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q415471"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C13473900&Units=SI")],
