            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Butyl acrylate is an organic compound with the formula C4H9O2CCH=CH2.  A colorless liquid, it is the butyl ester of acrylic acid.  It is used commercially on a large scale as a precursor to poly(butyl acrylate). Especially  as copolymers, such materials are used in paints, sealants, coatings, adhesives, fuel, textiles, plastics, and caulk."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H331: Toxic if inhaled [Danger Acute toxicity, inhalation]"),
            uses: ["Interior car care", "Monomers"],
            logp: Some(1.516),
            appearance: Some("Butyl acrylate appears as a clear colorless liquid with a sharp characteristic odor. Very slightly soluble in water and somewhat less dense than water. Hence forms surface slick on water. Flash point 105 °F. Density 7.5 lb / gal. Used for making paints, coatings, caulks, sealants, adhesives."),
            synonyms: ["n-Butyl acrylate", "Butyl-2-propenoate", "n-Butyl propenoate", "butyl prop-2-enoate", "Acrylic acid butyl ester", "Butyl ester of acrylic acid", "141-32-2", "2-Propenoic acid, butyl ester"],
