            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("1,1,3,3-Tetramethyl-1,3-divinyldisiloxane (also referred to as tetramethyldivinyldisiloxane) is the organosilicon compound with the formula O(SiMe2CH=CH2)2. 
Tetramethyldivinyldisiloxane is a colorless liquid that is employed as a ligand in organometallic chemistry and also as a homogeneous catalyst. The ligand is a component of Karstedt's catalyst. It was first prepared by hydrolysis of vinyldimethylmethoxysilane, (CH2=CH)Me2SiOMe."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H225 (94.3%): Highly Flammable liquid and vapor [Danger Flammable liquids]"),
            uses: ["Intermediate", "Monomers", "All Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "Intermediates"],
            logp: Some(2.864),
            appearance: Some("Liquid"),
            synonyms: ["1,3-Butanedithiol", "butane-1,3-dithiol", "2627-95-4", "1,1,3,3-Tetramethyl-1,3-divinyldisiloxane", "Disiloxane, 1,3-diethenyl-1,1,3,3-tetramethyl-", "Bisvinyltetramethyldisiloxane", "1,1'-Divinyltetramethyldisiloxane", "sym-Tetramethyldivinyldisiloxane"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=63645035"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/75819"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_179055"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q27289239"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C2627954&Units=SI")],
