            description: Some("Copper(II) nitrate describes any member of the family of inorganic compounds with the formula Cu(NO3)2·x(H2O). The hydrates are hygroscopic blue solids.  Anhydrous copper nitrate forms blue-green crystals and sublimes in a vacuum at 150–200 °C (302–392 °F). Common hydrates are the hemipentahydrate and trihydrate."),
