            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Bis(triethoxysilylpropyl)tetrasulfide is an organosulfur compound with the formula S4[C3H6Si(OEt)3]2 (Et = C2H5).  The molecule consists of two trialkoxysilyl propyl groups linked with a polysulfide.  It is often sold as a mixture with the trisulfide.  The compound is a colorless viscous liquid that is soluble in ordinary organic solvents such as toluene.  Commercial samples often are yellowish.  The compound is added to rubber compositions that contain silica filler."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
