            solubility_g_per_100ml_h2o: None,
            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Bronopol (INN; chemical name 2-bromo-2-nitropropane-1,3-diol) is an organic compound that is used as an antimicrobial. It is a white solid although commercial samples appear yellow.
The first reported synthesis of bronopol was in 1897.
Bronopol was invented by The Boots Company PLC in the early 1960s and first applications were as a preservative for pharmaceuticals. Due to its low mammalian toxicity at in-use levels and high activity against bacteria, especially Gram-negative species, bronopol became popular as a preservative in many consumer products such as shampoos and cosmetics. It was subsequently adopted as an antimicrobial in other industrial environments such as paper mills, oil exploration, and production facilities, as well as cooling water disinfection plants."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H318: Causes serious eye damage [Danger Serious eye damage/eye irritation]"),
            uses: ["Deodorizer", "Surfactant (surface active agent)", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "Biocide used in recirculating cooling towers"],
            logp: Some(-0.661),
            appearance: Some("2-bromo-2-nitropropane-1,3-diol appears as white crystals. Ignite easily and burn readily. May detonate under strong shock. Decomposes when heated, evolving toxic gases. Toxic by skin absorption, inhalation or ingestion."),
            synonyms: ["Bronopolu", "Bronopolum", "2-Bromo-2-nitropropane-1,3-diol", "2-Nitro-2-bromo-1,3-propanediol", "beta-Bromo-beta-nitrotrimethyleneglycol", "52-51-7", "2-Bromo-2-nitro-1,3-propanediol", "Bronosol"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=2406722"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/2450"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_31306"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2462902"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C52517&Units=SI")],
            element_info: None,
