            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Ricinine is a toxic alkaloid found in the castor plant. It can serve as a biomarker of ricin poisoning. It was first isolated from the castor seeds by Tuson in 1864.
Ricinine has insecticidal effects.
It sublimes between 170 and 180 °C at 20 mmHg. It does not form salts, and is precipitated in iodine or mercuric chloride solutions, but not in Mayer's reagent.
It can be hydrolyzed to methanol and ricininic acid by alkali."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H301 (100%): Toxic if swallowed [Danger Acute toxicity, oral]"),
            uses: [],
