            solubility_g_per_100ml_h2o: None,
            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Decamethylcyclopentasiloxane, also known as D5 and D5, is an organosilicon compound with the formula [(CH3)2SiO]5. It is a colorless and odorless liquid that is slightly volatile. It is used in various cosmetic products. It also is used as a dry cleaning solvent and has been marketed as an \"eco-friendly\" and \"green\" alternative to perchloroethylene in the 2000s, under the tradename GreenEarth. Decamethylcyclopentasiloxane is persistent in nature and bioaccumulative. Decamethylcyclopentasiloxane is acutely non-toxic but its long-term health effects are unknown."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H227: Combustible liquid [Warning Flammable liquids]"),
            uses: ["Adhesives and sealant chemicals", "Cleaning agent", "Diluent", "Intermediates", "Lubricants and lubricant additives", "Softener and conditioner"],
            logp: Some(3.592),
