            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Tibolone, sold under the brand name Livial among others, is a medication which is used in menopausal hormone therapy and in the treatment of postmenopausal osteoporosis and endometriosis. The medication is available alone and is not formulated or used in combination with other medications. It is taken by mouth.
Side effects of tibolone include acne and increased hair growth among others. Tibolone is a synthetic steroid with weak estrogenic, progestogenic, and androgenic activity, and hence is an agonist of the estrogen, progesterone, and androgen receptors. It is a prodrug of several metabolites. The estrogenic effects of tibolone may show tissue selectivity in their distribution.
Tibolone was developed in the 1960s and was introduced for medical use in 1988. It is marketed widely throughout the world. The medication is not available in the United States."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: None,
            uses: [],
            logp: Some(3.883),
            appearance: None,
            synonyms: ["TIB", "ORG-OD-14", "7α-Methylnoretynodrel", "7α-Methyl-17α-ethynyl-19-nor-δ5(10)-testosterone", "17α-Ethynyl-7α-methylestr-5(10)-en-17β-ol-3-one", "7α-Methyl-19-nor-17α-pregn-5(10)-en-20-yn-17-ol…", "5630-53-5", "Liviella"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=5162675"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C5630535&Units=SI")],
