            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Xylose (cf. Ancient Greek: ξύλον, xylon, \"wood\") is a common monosaccharide, i.e. a simple sugar. Xylose is classified as aldopentose type, which means that it contains five carbon atoms and includes an aldehyde functional group, at least in its open-chain form.  It is abundant in biomass, and is one of the most abundant sugars in nature.  It is a white, water-soluble solid."),
