            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Glycerol phenylbutyrate, sold under the brand name  Ravicti, is a nitrogen-binding agent medication used for chronic management of certain urea cycle disorders. The medication reduces the harmful buildup of ammonia in the body.  It functions as a prodrug  of phenylbutyric acid, which conjugates with glutamine  to form phenylacetylglutamine, facilitating ammonia excretion via the kidneys
It was developed by Hyperion Therapeutics based on the existing medication sodium phenylbutyrate, and received FDA approval in February 2013."),
