            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsMetal, IsAcid],
            description: Some("Sodium oxalate, or disodium oxalate, is a chemical compound with the chemical formula Na2C2O4. It is the sodium salt of oxalic acid. It contains sodium cations Na+ and oxalate anions C2O2−4. It is a white, crystalline, odorless solid, that decomposes above 290 °C.
Sodium oxalate can act as a reducing agent, and it may be used as a primary standard for standardizing potassium permanganate (KMnO4) solutions.
The mineral form of sodium oxalate is natroxalate. It is only very rarely found and restricted to extremely sodic conditions of ultra-alkaline pegmatites."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H318: Causes serious eye damage [Danger Serious eye damage/eye irritation]"),
