            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Amyl acetate (pentyl acetate) is an organic compound and an ester with the chemical formula CH3COO[CH2]4CH3 and the molecular weight 130.19 g/mol. It is colorless and has a scent similar to bananas and apples. The compound is the condensation product of acetic acid and 1-pentanol.  However, esters formed from other pentanol isomers (amyl alcohols), or mixtures of pentanols, are often referred to as amyl acetate. The symptoms of exposure to amyl acetate in humans are dermatitis, central nervous system depression, narcosis and irritation to the eyes and nose."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H372: Causes damage to organs through prolonged or repeated exposure [Danger Specific target organ toxicity, repeated exposure]"),
            uses: ["Fragrance", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "CIR ingredient: Amyl Acetate"],
            logp: Some(1.74),
            appearance: Some("N-amyl acetate appears as a mixture of isomers. A clear colorless liquid with a banana-like odor. Flash point varies from 65 °F to 95 °F. Less dense (at 7.2 lb / gal) than water and slightly soluble in water. Hence floats on water. Vapors heavier than air."),
            synonyms: ["amyl ethanoate", "n-amyl acetate", "pentyl acetate", "1-acetoxypentane", "1-pentyl acetate", "n-pentyl acetate", "pentyl ethanoate", "Amyl acetic ester"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=1829128"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/12348"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_87362"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q416972"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C628637&Units=SI")],
