            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Choline chloride is an organic compound with the formula [(CH3)3NCH2CH2OH]+Cl−. It is a quaternary ammonium salt, consisting of choline cations ([(CH3)3NCH2CH2OH]+) and chloride anions (Cl−). It is a bifunctional compound, meaning, it contains both a quaternary ammonium functional group and a hydroxyl functional group. The cation of this salt, choline, occurs in nature in living beings. Choline chloride is a white, water-soluble salt used mainly as an animal and human dietary supplement."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H315 (46%): Causes skin irritation [Warning Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
