            solubility_g_per_100ml_h2o: None,
            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsBase],
            description: Some("3,5-Dimethylpyrazole is an organic compound with the formula (CH3C)2CHN2H. It is one of several isomeric derivatives of pyrazole that contain two methyl substituents.  The compound is unsymmetrical but the corresponding conjugate acid (pyrazolium) and conjugate base (pyrazolide) have C2v symmetry. It is a white solid that dissolves well in polar organic solvents.
It is a precursor to a variety of ligands that are widely studied in coordination chemistry including trispyrazolylborate, a trispyrazolylmethane, and a pyrazolyldiphosphine. 
Condensation of acetylacetone and hydrazine gives 3,5-dimethylpyrazole:

CH3C(O)CH2C(O)CH3   +   N2H4   →   (CH3C)2CHN2H   +   2 H2O
It has found use as a blocking agent for isocyanates."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H360: May damage fertility or the unborn child [Danger Reproductive toxicity]"),
            uses: ["All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "Intermediate", "Paint and Coating Manufacturing", "Pharmaceutical and Medicine Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(1.027),
            appearance: Some("Pellets or Large Crystals"),
            synonyms: ["3,5-dimethyl-1H-pyrazole", "67-51-6", "1H-Pyrazole, 3,5-dimethyl-", "PYRAZOLE, 3,5-DIMETHYL-", "3,5 DMP", "TH 564", "U 6245", "H21N865K9J"],
