            properties: [],
            description: Some("Pralidoxime (2-pyridine aldoxime methyl chloride) or 2-PAM, usually as the chloride or iodide salts, belongs to a family of compounds called oximes that bind to organophosphate-inactivated acetylcholinesterase.  It is used to treat organophosphate poisoning in conjunction with atropine and either diazepam or midazolam. It is a white solid."),
