            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("N-Cyclohexyl-2-pyrrolidone or CHP is a yellow to colorless liquid. It has a low vapor pressure, and is nearly odorless. It has a low solubility in water, but is soluble in a variety of organic solvents.
CHP is used in the electronics industry as a photoresist stripper (usually in combination with other solvents like N-methyl-2-pyrrolidone), and as a chemical polisher of copper in circuit board fabrication. It is also used in the textiles industry as a dye carrier in aramid fabrics."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H314 (98.7%): Causes severe skin burns and eye damage [Danger Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
            uses: ["Solvents (for cleaning or degreasing)", "Synthetic Dye and Pigment Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(1.941),
            appearance: Some("Liquid"),
            synonyms: ["N-Octyl-2-pyrrolidone", "1-octylpyrrolidin-2-one", "6837-24-7", "1-cyclohexylpyrrolidin-2-one", "N-Cyclohexyl-2-pyrrolidone", "2-Pyrrolidinone, 1-cyclohexyl-", "N-Cyclohexylpyrrolidone", "Cyclohexyl pyrrolidone"],
