            properties: [],
            description: Some("Sulfur trioxide (alternative spelling sulphur trioxide) is the chemical compound with the formula SO3. It has been described as \"unquestionably the most [economically] important sulfur oxide\". It is prepared on an industrial scale as a precursor to sulfuric acid.
Sulfur trioxide exists in several forms: gaseous monomer, crystalline trimer, and solid polymer. Sulfur trioxide is a solid at just below room temperature with a relatively narrow liquid range. Gaseous SO3 is the primary precursor to acid rain."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H314 (85.1%): Causes severe skin burns and eye damage [Danger Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
            uses: ["Intermediates", "Agricultural chemicals (non-pesticidal)", "Agriculture, Forestry, Fishing and Hunting", "All Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(-1.004),
