            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Chloral, also known as trichloroacetaldehyde or trichloroethanal, is the organic compound with the formula Cl3CCHO. This aldehyde is a colourless liquid that is soluble in a wide range of solvents. It reacts with water to form chloral hydrate, a once widely used sedative and hypnotic substance."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H330 (13.5%): Fatal if inhaled [Danger Acute toxicity, inhalation]"),
            uses: ["Agricultural chemicals (non-pesticidal)", "Manufacture of chloral hydrate and DDT.", "USED IN SPRAYING & POURING OF POLYURETHANES."],
            logp: Some(1.556),
            appearance: Some("Trichloroacetaldehyde appears as a colorless oily liquid with a penetrating odor. Reacts with water and denser than water. Contact may irritate skin, eyes and mucous membranes. Toxic by ingestion and inhalation. Used to make pesticides."),
            synonyms: ["Noctec", "Somnote", "Chloralhydrat", "knockout drops", "Chloral hydrate", "chloral monohydrate", "Aquachloral Supprettes", "Tri-Chloro-Acetaldehyde"],
