            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsMetal, IsAcid],
            description: Some("Sodium metabisulfite or sodium pyrosulfite (IUPAC spelling; Br. E. sodium metabisulphite or sodium pyrosulphite) is an inorganic compound of chemical formula Na2S2O5.  The substance is sometimes referred to as disodium metabisulfite.  It is used as a disinfectant, antioxidant, and preservative agent. When dissolved in water it forms sodium bisulfite."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H318: Causes serious eye damage [Danger Serious eye damage/eye irritation]"),
            uses: ["Bleaching agent", "Flotation agent", "Processing aids, not otherwise listed", "Reducing agent", "Solvents (for cleaning or degreasing)"],
            logp: Some(-1.37),
            appearance: Some("Sodium metabisulfite appears as a white crystalline or powder solid with a slight sulfur odor. Toxic by inhalation. Strongly irritates skin and tissue. Noncombustible, but may decompose to emit toxic oxide fumes of sulfur and sodium when heated to high temperature. A corrosive acid when mixed with water. Used as a food preservative and as a laboratory reagent."),
            synonyms: ["E223", "Na2S2O5", "sodium disulfite", "Disodium disulfite", "Disodium disulphite", "sodium pyrosulphite", "Disodium pyrosulfite", "sodium metabisulfite"],
