            enthalpy_formation_kj_mol: None,
            solubility_g_per_100ml_h2o: None,
            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsAcid],
            description: Some("Citric acid is an organic compound with the formula C6H8O7. It is a colorless weak organic acid. It occurs naturally in citrus fruits. In biochemistry, it is an intermediate in the citric acid cycle, which occurs in the metabolism of all aerobic organisms.
More than two million tons of citric acid are manufactured every year. It is used widely as acidifier, flavoring, preservative, and chelating agent.
A citrate is a derivative of citric acid; that is, the salts, esters, and the polyatomic anion found in solutions and salts of citric acid. An example of the former, a salt is trisodium citrate; an ester is triethyl citrate. When citrate trianion is part of a salt, the formula of the citrate trianion is written as C6H5O3−7 or C3H5O(COO)3−3."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H319: Causes serious eye irritation [Warning Serious eye damage/eye irritation]"),
            uses: ["Agricultural chemicals (non-pesticidal)", "Binder", "Chelating agent", "Cleaning agent", "Hardener", "Lubricants and lubricant additives"],
            logp: Some(-1.248),
            appearance: Some("Citric acid appears as colorless, odorless crystals with an acid taste. Denser than water. (USCG, 1999)"),
            synonyms: ["E330", "E 330", "H3cit", "Citronensaeure", "anhydrous citric acid", "2-Hydroxytricarballylic acid", "beta-hydroxytricarballylic acid", "2-Hydroxy-1,2,3-propanetricarboxylic acid"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=54536"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/311"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_30769"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q159683"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C77929&Units=SI")],
            element_info: None,
        ),
