            enthalpy_formation_kj_mol: None,
            solubility_g_per_100ml_h2o: None,
            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Potassium perchlorate is the inorganic salt with the chemical formula KClO4. Like other perchlorates, this salt is a strong oxidizer when the solid is heated at high temperature, although it usually reacts very slowly in solution with reducing agents or organic substances. This colorless crystalline solid is a common oxidizer used in fireworks, ammunition percussion caps, and explosive primers, and is used variously in propellants, flash compositions, stars, and sparklers. It has been used as a solid rocket propellant, although in that application it has mostly been replaced by the more performant ammonium perchlorate.
KClO4 has a relatively low solubility in water (1.5 g in 100 mL of water at 25 °C)."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H271: May cause fire or explosion; strong Oxidizer [Danger Oxidizing liquids; Oxidizing solids]"),
            uses: ["Propellants and blowing agents", "All Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing", "Explosives Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(-4.505),
            appearance: Some("Potassium perchlorate appears as a white crystalline solid. Forms explosive mixtures with certain combustible materials. Difficult to burn, but will accelerate burning of combustible materials. Prolonged exposure to fire or heat may result in an explosion. Used in explosives, pyrotechnics, photography."),
            synonyms: ["ClO4(-)", "[ClO4](-)", "Perchlorat", "perchlorate", "Chlorat(VII)", "PERCHLORATE ION", "tetraoxochlorate", "tetraoxochlorate(1-)"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=1024033"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/45051740"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_49706"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q422434"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C7778747&Units=SI")],
            element_info: None,
        ),
