            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Magnesium chloride is an inorganic compound with the formula MgCl2. It forms hydrates MgCl2·nH2O, where n can range from 1 to 12. These salts are colorless or white solids that are highly soluble in water. These compounds and their solutions, both of which occur in nature, have a variety of practical uses. Anhydrous magnesium chloride is the principal precursor to magnesium metal, which is produced on a large scale. Hydrated magnesium chloride is the form most readily available."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H318 (27.6%): Causes serious eye damage [Danger Serious eye damage/eye irritation]"),
