            properties: [IsAcid],
            description: Some("Fluorosulfuric acid (IUPAC name: sulfurofluoridic acid) is the inorganic compound with the chemical formula HSO3F. It is one of the strongest acids commercially available. It is a tetrahedral molecule and is closely related to sulfuric acid, H2SO4, substituting a fluorine atom for one of the hydroxyl groups. It is a colourless liquid, although commercial samples are often yellow."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H314: Causes severe skin burns and eye damage [Danger Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
            uses: ["Catalyst", "IN ELECTROPOLISHING"],
            logp: Some(-0.241),
            appearance: Some("Fluorosulfonic acid appears as a fuming liquid. Boiling point 163 °C. Density 1.73 g / cm3. Corrosive to metals and to tissue. Both very short contact and the fumes can cause severe painful burns. Used as a catalyst in organic synthesis, in electroplating and as a fluorinating agent."),
            synonyms: ["fluorosulfonic acid", "sulfurofluoridic acid", "perfluorosulfonic acid", "monofluorosulfuric acid", "7789-21-1", "Fluosulfuric acid", "FLUOSULFONIC ACID", "Fluorosulphonic acid"],
