            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Tetraethyl orthosilicate, formally named tetraethoxysilane (TEOS), ethyl silicate is the organic chemical compound with the formula Si(OC2H5)4.  TEOS is a colorless liquid. It degrades in water.  TEOS is the ethyl ester of orthosilicic acid, Si(OH)4.  It is the most prevalent alkoxide of silicon.
TEOS is a tetrahedral molecule. Like its many analogues, it is prepared by alcoholysis of silicon tetrachloride:

SiCl4  +  4 EtOH → Si(OEt)4  +  4 HCl
where Et is the ethyl group, C2H5, and thus EtOH is ethanol."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H370: Causes damage to organs [Danger Specific target organ toxicity, single exposure]"),
            uses: ["Adhesives and sealant chemicals", "Binder", "All Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "Construction"],
            logp: Some(1.568),
            appearance: Some("Ethyl silicate appears as a clear colorless liquid with a faint odor. Flash point 125 °F. Less dense than water. Vapors are heavier than air."),
            synonyms: ["ethyl silicate", "ethyl orthosilicate", "tetraethyl orthosilicate", "Tetraethyl silicate", "78-10-4", "TEOS", "Dynasil A", "Silicon ethoxide"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=10942079"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/6517"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q421458"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C78104&Units=SI")],
