            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Azobisisobutyronitrile (abbreviated AIBN) is an organic compound with the formula [(CH3)2C(CN)]2N2. This white powder is soluble in alcohols and common organic solvents but is insoluble in water. It is often used as a foamer in plastics and rubber and as a radical initiator. 
As an azo initiator, radicals resulting from AIBN have multiple benefits over common organic peroxides. For example, they do not have oxygenated byproducts or much yellow discoloration. Additionally, they do not cause too much grafting and therefore are often used when making adhesives, acrylic fibers, detergents, etc."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H242: Heating may cause a fire [Danger Self-reactive substances and mixtures; Organic peroxides]"),
            uses: ["Photosensitive chemicals", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "Flame retardants"],
            logp: Some(2.043),
            appearance: None,
            synonyms: ["78-67-1", "2,2'-Azobis(2-methylpropionitrile)", "Azdh", "Porofor N", "Aceto AZIB", "Pianofor an", "Porofor 57", "Azobis(isobutyronitrile)"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=2231865"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/6547"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q126677498"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C78671&Units=SI")],
