            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Isobutyraldehyde is the chemical compound with the formula (CH3)2CHCHO. It is an aldehyde, isomeric with n-butyraldehyde (butanal). Isobutyraldehyde is made, often as a side-product, by the hydroformylation of propene. Its odour is described as that of wet cereal or straw. It undergoes the Cannizzaro reaction even though it has alpha hydrogen atom. It is a colorless volatile liquid."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H225 (100%): Highly Flammable liquid and vapor [Danger Flammable liquids]"),
            uses: ["Hardener", "Intermediate", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(0.841),
            appearance: Some("Isobutyl aldehyde appears as a clear colorless liquid with a pungent odor. Flash point of -40 °F. Less dense than water and insoluble in water. Hence floats on water. Vapors are heavier than air. Used to make other chemicals."),
            synonyms: ["isobutanal", "isobutyral", "isobutaldehyde", "methylpropanal", "isobutyraldehyd", "methyl propanal", "2-methylpropanal", "isobutylaldehyde"],
