            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsAcid],
            description: Some("Isobutyric acid, also known as 2-methylpropanoic acid or isobutanoic acid, is a carboxylic acid with structural formula (CH3)2CHCOOH. It is an isomer of butyric acid. It is classified as a short-chain fatty acid. Deprotonation or esterification gives derivatives called isobutyrates.
Isobutyric acid is a colorless liquid with a somewhat unpleasant odor.  It is soluble in water and organic solvents.  It is found naturally in carobs (Ceratonia siliqua), in vanilla, and in the root of Arnica dulcis, and as an ethyl ester in croton oil."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H311 (11.3%): Toxic in contact with skin [Danger Acute toxicity, dermal]"),
            uses: ["All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "Food and animal feed fungistat /Former use/", "Intermediate"],
            logp: Some(0.727),
            appearance: Some("Isobutyric acid appears as a colorless liquid with a light odor of rancid butter. Corrosive to metals and tissue."),
            synonyms: ["Isobutyrate", "Isobutanoate", "iso-C3H7COOH", "i-butyric acid", "Isobuttersaeure", "iso-butyric acid", "isobutanoic acid", "2-Methylpropanoate"],
