            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Trichloroisocyanuric acid is an organic compound with the formula (CONCl)3.  It is used as an industrial disinfectant, bleaching agent and a reagent in organic synthesis. This white crystalline powder, which has a strong \"chlorine odour,\" is sometimes sold in tablet or granule form for domestic and industrial use."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H272: May intensify fire; oxidizer [Danger Oxidizing liquids; Oxidizing solids]"),
            uses: ["Bleaching agent", "Fumigant"],
            logp: Some(-0.823),
            appearance: Some("Trichloro-s-triazinetrione, dry appears as a white slightly hygroscopic crystalline powder or lump solid with a mild chlorine-like odor. Said to have 85 percent available chlorine. Decomposes at 225 °C. Moderately toxic by ingestion. May irritate skin and eyes. Active ingredient in household dry bleaches. Used in swimming pools as a disinfectant."),
            synonyms: ["TCCA", "Symclosene", "trichlorocyanuric acid", "trichloroiminocyanuric acid", "1,3,5-trichloro-1,3,5-triazinane-2,4,6-trione", "1,3,5-trichloro-1,3,5-triazine-2,4,6(1H,3H,5H)-…", "87-90-1", "Symclosen"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=5122292"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/6909"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_33015"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q419127"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C87901&Units=SI")],
