            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsBase],
            description: Some("Phenothiazine, abbreviated PTZ, is an organic compound that has the formula S(C6H4)2NH and is related to the thiazine-class of heterocyclic compounds.  Derivatives of phenothiazine are highly bioactive and have widespread use.
The derivatives chlorpromazine and promethazine revolutionized the fields of psychiatry and allergy treatment, respectively. An earlier derivative, methylene blue, was one of the first antimalarial drugs, and derivatives of phenothiazine are currently under investigation as possible anti-infective drugs.  Phenothiazine is a prototypical pharmaceutical lead structure in medicinal chemistry."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H370: Causes damage to organs [Danger Specific target organ toxicity, single exposure]"),
            uses: ["Hydraulic fluids", "Oxidizing/reducing agents", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "Binder", "Defoamer"],
            logp: Some(3.895),
            appearance: Some("Phenothiazine is a light green to steel-blue powder. Acquires a greenish-brown tint under exposure to sunlight. (NTP, 1992)"),
            synonyms: ["Phenothiazin", "fenothiazine", "dibenzothiazine", "10H-Phenothiazin", "thiodiphenylamine", "dibenzo-1,4-thiazine", "10H-Phenothiazine", "92-84-2"],
