            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("1,2-Dichlorobenzene, or orthodichlorobenzene (ODCB), is an aryl chloride and isomer of dichlorobenzene with the formula C6H4Cl2. This colourless liquid is poorly soluble in water but miscible with most organic solvents. It is a derivative of benzene, substituted with two adjacent chlorine atoms.
It is mainly used as a precursor chemical in the synthesis of agrochemicals, as a preferred solvent for dissolving and working with fullerenes, as an insecticide, and in softening and removing carbon-based contamination on metal surfaces."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H331: Toxic if inhaled [Danger Acute toxicity, inhalation]"),
            uses: ["Solvent", "Intermediate"],
            logp: Some(2.993),
            appearance: Some("O-dichlorobenzene appears as a clear colorless liquid with a pleasant odor. Denser than water and insoluble in water. Flash point 150 °F. Toxic by inhalation and ingestion. Used to make other chemicals, solvents, fumigants and insecticides and for many other uses."),
            synonyms: ["ODB", "ODCB", "o-DCB", "o-Dichlorbenzol", "o-Dichlorobenzol", "o-dichlorbenzene", "2-Dichlorobenzene", "o-Dichlorobenzene"],
