            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsAcid],
            description: Some("γ-Butyrolactone (GBL) or gamma-butyrolactone is an organic compound with the formula O=CO(CH2)3. It is a hygroscopic, colorless, water-miscible liquid with a pleasant odor. It is the simplest 4-carbon lactone. It is mainly used as an intermediate in the production of other chemicals, such as N-methyl-2-pyrrolidone.
In humans, GBL acts as a prodrug for gamma-hydroxybutyric acid (GHB) and is often used as a recreational drug. GHB acts as a central nervous system (CNS) depressant with effects similar to those of barbiturates."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H318 (68.3%): Causes serious eye damage [Danger Serious eye damage/eye irritation]"),
