            description: Some("Isobutyric anhydride is an organic compound with the formula ((CH3)2CHCO)2O. It is an acyclic carboxylic anhydride of isobutyric acid. It is classified as an organic acid anhydride, being derived from dehydration of isobutyric acid.  It is a colorless liquid with a strong, pungent odor.
Isobutyric anhydride is a reagent in the production of the ester of cyclohexanone oxime."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H301 (17.3%): Toxic if swallowed [Danger Acute toxicity, oral]"),
            uses: ["All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "CHEMICAL INTERMEDIATE", "Intermediate", "Patented for use as flavor and/or aroma enhancer"],
            logp: Some(1.368),
            appearance: Some("Isobutyric anhydride appears as a colorless liquid. Burns skin and eyes. Vapors are heavier than air."),
            synonyms: ["isobutyric acid anhydride", "2-methylpropanoic anhydride", "2-methylpropanoyl 2-methylpropanoate", "2-methylpropionic acid isobutyryl ester", "97-72-3", "Propanoic acid, 2-methyl-, anhydride", "Isobutyryl anhydride", "2-Methylpropionic anhydride"],
