            description: Some("Tetrahydrofurfuryl alcohol (THFA) is an organic compound with the formula HOCH2C4H7O.  In terms of its structure, it consists of a tetrahydrofuran ring substituted in the 2-position with a hydroxymethyl group.  It is a colorless liquid that is used as a specialty solvent and synthetic intermediate, e.g. to 3,4-dihydropyran.  It is prepared by hydrogenation of furfural.  It is a precursor to 1,5-pentanediol."),
