            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsBase],
            description: Some("Bis(trimethylsilyl)amine (also known as hexamethyldisilazane and HMDS) is an organosilicon compound with the molecular formula [(CH3)3Si]2NH. The molecule is a derivative of ammonia with trimethylsilyl groups in place of two hydrogen atoms. An electron diffraction study shows that silicon-nitrogen bond length (173.5 pm) and Si-N-Si bond angle (125.5°) to be similar to disilazane (in which methyl groups are replaced by hydrogen atoms) suggesting that steric factors are not a factor in regulating angles in this case. This colorless liquid is a reagent and a precursor to bases that are popular in organic synthesis and organometallic chemistry. Additionally, HMDS is also increasingly used as molecular precursor in chemical vapor deposition techniques to deposit silicon carbonitride thin films or coatings."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H225 (93.7%): Highly Flammable liquid and vapor [Danger Flammable liquids]"),
            uses: ["Intermediate", "Polymerization promoter", "Adhesion/cohesion promoter", "Adhesive Manufacturing", "Adhesives and sealant chemicals", "All Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(2.246),
            appearance: Some("Hexamethyl disilazane appears as a liquid. May be toxic by ingestion. Irritates skin and eyes. Vapors are heavier than air. May emit highly toxic nitrogen oxide fumes when heated to decomposition. Used to make other chemicals."),
            synonyms: ["HMDS", "(TMS)2NH", "((CH3)3Si)2NH", "Hexamethylsilazane", "Bis(trimethylsilyl)amine", "1,1,1,3,3,3-Hexamethyldisilazane", "Trimethyl-N-(trimethylsilyl)silanamine", "1,1,1-trimethyl-N-(trimethylsilyl)silanamine"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=6606771"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/13838"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_85068"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q425001"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C999973&Units=SI")],
            element_info: None,
        ),
